  m_Name: 1800s thaipusam
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Thaipusam Festival 19th Century
  info: "Brought by Tamil immigrants, Thaipusam is a Hindu festival dedicated to
    Lord Murugan. Devotees participate in elaborate rituals, carrying kavadis adorned
    with flowers, spikes, and milk pots, or piercing their bodies as acts of penance
    and devotion. The vibrant processions and spiritual significance highlight the
    rich traditions of Singapore\u2019s Indian community.  "
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cce8898b6e8aa4da6bb90f5e956f42e7, type: 3}
